# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Submit the problem through the Qiskit Function. The Qiskit Functions Catalog handles IBM Quantum authentication, so you don't pass separate Fire Opal or hardware-provider credentials to `sim_qf.run()`.\n"
msgstr "I-submit ang problema sa pamamagitan ng Qiskit Function. Ang Qiskit Functions Catalog ang humahawak ng IBM Quantum authentication, kaya hindi mo na kailangang magpasa ng hiwalay na Fire Opal o hardware-provider credentials sa `sim_qf.run()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The returned object is a Qiskit Function job. You can keep the job ID to retrieve or inspect the workload later.\n"
msgstr "Ang ibinalik na object ay isang Qiskit Function job. Puwede mong itago ang job ID para makuha o masilip ang workload mamaya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Retrieve the result {#3-retrieve-the-result}"
msgstr "3. Kunin ang resulta {#3-retrieve-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the observable expectation values to a NumPy array. Each row corresponds to one observable, and each column corresponds to a recorded simulation time, beginning at $t=0$. For this example, the four rows contain the spin-up occupations of sites 0 through 3.\n"
msgstr "I-convert ang mga expectation value ng observable sa isang NumPy array. Ang bawat row ay tumutugma sa isang observable, at ang bawat column ay tumutugma sa isang naitalang simulation time, simula sa $t=0$. Sa halimbawang ito, ang apat na row ay naglalaman ng spin-up occupation ng mga site 0 hanggang 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Visualize the dynamics {#4-visualize-the-dynamics}"
msgstr "4. I-visualize ang dynamics {#4-visualize-the-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state contains one spin-up fermion and no spin-down fermions. Its evolution therefore remains in the single-particle subspace, whose four basis states correspond to the fermion occupying sites 0, 1, 2, and 3.\n"
msgstr "Ang initial state ay may isang spin-up fermion at walang spin-down fermion. Kaya ang ebolusyon nito ay nananatili sa single-particle subspace, na ang apat na basis state ay tumutugma sa fermion na nasa site 0, 1, 2, at 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this subspace, the Hamiltonian connects neighboring sites with hopping amplitude $-t_h$. For the parameters used here,\n"
msgstr "Sa subspace na ito, ikinokonekta ng Hamiltonian ang magkakatabing site gamit ang hopping amplitude na $-t_h$. Para sa mga parameter na ginamit dito,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathrm{1p}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathrm{1p}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"-t_h\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"-t_h\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize this matrix with NumPy and evolve the initial state at the same times that were returned by the Dynamics Simulator. The squared magnitude of each state amplitude gives the spin-up occupation of the corresponding site.\n"
msgstr "I-diagonalize ang matrix na ito gamit ang NumPy at i-evolve ang initial state sa parehong mga oras na ibinalik ng Dynamics Simulator. Ang squared magnitude ng bawat state amplitude ang nagbibigay ng spin-up occupation ng katumbas na site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This calculation gives exact Hamiltonian evolution. Differences between the hardware estimates and this reference can include the finite Trotter step, measurement statistics, and residual hardware errors.\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang kalkulasyong ito ng eksaktong Hamiltonian evolution. Ang mga pagkakaiba ng hardware estimate at ng reference na ito ay maaaring manggaling sa finite Trotter step, measurement statistics, at natitirang hardware error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot one panel for each site. The solid curves show the exact reference at the recorded times, and the markers show the hardware estimates returned by the Dynamics Simulator.\n"
msgstr "Mag-plot ng isang panel para sa bawat site. Ipinapakita ng mga solid na kurba ang eksaktong reference sa mga naitalang oras, at ipinapakita ng mga marker ang hardware estimate na ibinalik ng Dynamics Simulator.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/extracted-outputs/61a7ad6e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/extracted-outputs/61a7ad6e-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At $t=0$, the exact spin-up occupation is 1 at site 0 and 0 at the other sites. As the system evolves, hopping spreads the particle's probability across the chain. The occupation of site 1 increases first, followed by increasing occupation at sites 2 and 3. For the parameters in this example, the final recorded time is $t=1.6$. The exact occupations of sites 0 through 3 are approximately 0.026, 0.370, 0.392, and 0.211, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Sa $t=0$, ang eksaktong spin-up occupation ay 1 sa site 0 at 0 sa iba pang site. Habang nag-e-evolve ang sistema, ikinakalat ng hopping ang probability ng particle sa buong chain. Unang tumataas ang occupation ng site 1, sunod ang pagtaas ng occupation sa mga site 2 at 3. Para sa mga parameter sa halimbawang ito, ang huling naitalang oras ay $t=1.6$. Ang eksaktong occupation ng mga site 0 hanggang 3 ay humigit-kumulang 0.026, 0.370, 0.392, at 0.211, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact occupations satisfy the following equation at every time, reflecting conservation of particle number:\n"
msgstr "Natutugunan ng eksaktong occupation ang sumusunod na equation sa bawat oras, na sumasalamin sa conservation ng bilang ng particle:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=0}^{3}\\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t)\\rangle=1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=0}^{3}\\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t)\\rangle=1\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual site occupations can rise and fall as the particle evolves through the finite chain.\n"
msgstr "Ang occupation ng bawat site ay puwedeng tumaas at bumaba habang gumagalaw ang particle sa finite chain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch error messages {#fetch-error-messages}"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga error message {#fetch-error-messages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workload enters the `ERROR` state, call `job.result()` to retrieve the error message. You can also inspect the function logs, if they are available.\n"
msgstr "Kung pumasok ang workload sa `ERROR` state, tawagin ang `job.result()` para makuha ang error message. Puwede mo ring silipin ang function logs, kung available ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common input-validation issues include an unsupported model or simulation method, an initial-state string that is too long, mismatched observable terms and coefficients, or an observable that references a site outside the initial-state string.\n"
msgstr "Kabilang sa mga karaniwang isyu sa input validation ang hindi suportadong model o simulation method, initial-state string na masyadong mahaba, hindi magkatugmang observable term at coefficient, o observable na tumutukoy sa site na wala sa initial-state string.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get support {#get-support}"
msgstr "Humingi ng suporta {#get-support}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For questions about the Dynamics Simulator or Fire Opal behavior, see the [Q-CTRL documentation](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/) or [contact Q-CTRL](https://form.typeform.com/to/iuujEAEI).\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga tanong tungkol sa Dynamics Simulator o sa behavior ng Fire Opal, tingnan ang [Q-CTRL documentation](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/) o [makipag-ugnayan sa Q-CTRL](https://form.typeform.com/to/iuujEAEI).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Qiskit Functions authentication, job management, or IBM Quantum Platform access, see the [Qiskit Functions documentation](/guides/functions).\n"
msgstr "Para sa Qiskit Functions authentication, job management, o access sa IBM Quantum Platform, tingnan ang [Qiskit Functions documentation](/guides/functions).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Review the [`simulate_dynamics` API reference](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/references/fire-opal/fireopal/fireopal.simulate_dynamics) for the underlying model, simulation, observable, output, and validation definitions.\n"
"- Try the [Spin and charge dynamics in the Fermi-Hubbard model](/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics) tutorial.\n"
"- Read the [Fire Opal dynamics simulator overview](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/fire-opal/execute/run-algorithms/fire-opal-dynamics-simulator) for more detail about Trotterization, hardware-aware mapping, and Fire Opal error suppression.\n"
"- Modify the model parameters, initial state, time step, step count, and observables to study a different one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard dynamics problem.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- Tingnan ang [`simulate_dynamics` API reference](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/references/fire-opal/fireopal/fireopal.simulate_dynamics) para sa mga definition ng pinagbabatayang model, simulation, observable, output, at validation.\n"
"- Subukan ang tutorial na [Spin and charge dynamics in the Fermi-Hubbard model](/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics).\n"
"- Basahin ang [Fire Opal dynamics simulator overview](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/fire-opal/execute/run-algorithms/fire-opal-dynamics-simulator) para sa karagdagang detalye tungkol sa Trotterization, hardware-aware mapping, at Fire Opal error suppression.\n"
"- Baguhin ang mga model parameter, initial state, time step, bilang ng step, at mga observable para pag-aralan ang ibang one-dimensional na Fermi-Hubbard dynamics problem.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
